WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:02.365
(whimsical music)

00:00:02.365 --> 00:00:05.467
- These Santas are all
really kids at heart.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.696
They like the fun and
laughter that comes with it,

00:00:07.696 --> 00:00:10.419
and making people happy;
that's why we're here.

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:12.474
If you ask 'em why their Santa,
most of 'em will tell you

00:00:12.474 --> 00:00:15.073
because they enjoyed being a child,

00:00:15.073 --> 00:00:16.607
so they're going back to that.

00:00:16.607 --> 00:00:19.273
They're reliving their childhood.

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:20.249
It's a wonderful thing.

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:22.283
(applause)

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:25.100
Welcome everyone to the Charles W. Howard

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.715
80th anniversary Santa Claus School.

00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:29.965
(cheering)

00:00:35.771 --> 00:00:37.591
♪ You better watch out ♪

00:00:37.591 --> 00:00:39.187
♪ You better not cry ♪

00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:40.558
♪ You better not put ♪

00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:42.806
♪ I'm telling you why ♪

00:00:42.806 --> 00:00:43.796
♪ Santa Claus ♪

00:00:43.796 --> 00:00:45.368
♪ Is coming ♪

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:47.535
♪ To town ♪

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.998
(cheering)

00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:53.992
- My name's Tom Valent.

00:00:53.992 --> 00:00:56.224
I'm the Dean of the Charles W. Howard

00:00:56.224 --> 00:00:59.641
Santa Claus School in Midland, Michigan.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.943
This is the Harvard of Santa schools.

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:09.014
This is the oldest-running Santa
Claus school in the world.

00:01:09.014 --> 00:01:12.431
It was started by Charlie Howard in 1937.

00:01:13.847 --> 00:01:15.901
At Santa Claus school we learn everything

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:19.570
from beard keeping to personal hygiene.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:22.787
- What we're gonna do, we're
gonna start with a base.

00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:25.311
- [Tom] To toy making,
to what it feels like

00:01:25.311 --> 00:01:27.096
to ride on the Polar Express.

00:01:27.096 --> 00:01:29.847
(laughing merrily)

00:01:29.847 --> 00:01:31.597
To flying the sleigh.

00:01:33.256 --> 00:01:35.708
- I want us to not be afraid of dance.

00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:37.609
- [Tom] Santa has to be healthy.

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:38.899
He's a healthy outdoorsman.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:41.713
If you're not healthy,
you're gonna drift off,

00:01:41.713 --> 00:01:43.912
you're not gonna pay attention.

00:01:43.912 --> 00:01:46.571
It's very important to
have all the skills you can

00:01:46.571 --> 00:01:48.757
to be a great Santa, because the child

00:01:48.757 --> 00:01:52.009
is gonna remember this visit
for the rest of your life.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:52.926
- Ho ho ho!

00:01:54.094 --> 00:01:55.427
Merry Christmas!

00:01:58.676 --> 00:01:59.737
- [Tom] When Charlie had this school,

00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:01.609
he had three or four students,

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:04.017
in good years, maybe 15 students.

00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:06.729
This year, we have 214.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:07.896
It just grows.

00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:11.590
We have Santa's of course
from almost every state

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:12.973
in the United States.

00:02:12.973 --> 00:02:16.212
We have around 20 Santas from Canada.

00:02:16.212 --> 00:02:19.024
We have three Santas from Denmark,

00:02:19.024 --> 00:02:22.191
one from Norway, and one from Germany.

00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:26.158
There's a real sense of
camaraderie in this school.

00:02:26.158 --> 00:02:29.360
It's like this large Santa
family coming together.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.420
They share stories, they
learn from each other.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.159
We want to be Santas to make people happy.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:36.815
Well when we get together
we're making each other happy.

00:02:36.815 --> 00:02:37.648
I love it!

00:02:39.387 --> 00:02:40.728
Once they leave this school,

00:02:40.728 --> 00:02:44.217
I hope that each and every
Santa and Mrs. Claus

00:02:44.217 --> 00:02:47.257
goes out and spreads
the spirit of Christmas,

00:02:47.257 --> 00:02:50.819
spreads the love and joy that
we have here at this school,

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:54.409
and passes it on to all
the little children,

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:56.097
and all the families.

00:02:56.097 --> 00:02:59.576
When you give joy, you
get it back two-fold.

00:02:59.576 --> 00:03:01.909
(hollering)

